Karl beat me too it.  Sorry, I think the lower-case "p" was my typo.
Your clue was that while "gt[ gt$P.value < 1e-4, ] " created nice
output for the screen, the command "suspect.marker.table <- gt[ gt
$p.value < 1e-4, ] " which should do the same thing but place the
output in an object "suspect.marker.table" created an empty object.
Since the only difference should be the assignment operator, something
had to be wrong with that line.

