Hi

I am just wondering what threshhold i should choose to get real QTLs. As my population is F7 with 98 individuals and 357 markers. Whereas I have choosen cofactors Individual - 12. But sometime I get genetic map with too many cofactors which makes me suspect the result.

I am biologist so cant think in depth what threshold would be good to get reliable qtls.

Thanks in advance

config.txt

#Global parameters

memorylimitN = 2048

maindir = D:/R_MQM_tomato

verbose = false

#Input Files

datafileraw = All_Marker.csv

datafilenormalized = All_Trans_Marker.csv crosstype = riself

#Output Files

resultfile = TabulatedResultFile.csv

tablesep = ;

imageoutput = png

imagewidthI = 800

imageheightI = 600

#Qtl mapping method (0=only mqm, 1=mqm compared against scanone/two) mapmethodI = 1 stepsizeN = 10 windowsizeN= 20 cofactorfile = cof.txt setalfaN = 0.02

#Permutation

npermutationsI = 100

ncoresI = 2

interactionstrenghtN = 4

#What to do

plothistogram = on

ploteffects = on

plotinteractions = on

plotcircles = on

circlespacingI = 200

plotheatmap = on

plotclusteredheatmap = on

plotclustergroups = on

clustergroupcutoffI = 25

